SUMMARY:What Are People For: Design Philosophy by Patrick Whitney
LOCATION:MIT\, 134 MASSACHUSETTS Avenue\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:What Are People For: Design Philosophy by Patrick Whitney Bosto
 n-Cambridge Premiere of Gary Hustwit’s New Film and Interactive Design W
 orkshop Join the Morningside Academy of Design for the Boston-Cambridge Pr
 emiere of What Are People For: Design Philosophy by Patrick Whitney\, the 
 latest short film by acclaimed design documentarian Gary Hustwit (Helvetic
 a\, Objectified\, Urbanized\, Eno)\, and interactive design workshop on Oc
 tober 24th. Explore how design can address today's most complex challenges
  from 2-5pm with a hands-on workshop led by Evan Chan and André Nogueira.
  Chan and Nogueira will introduce the Whole View model\, a systems design 
 approach for reframing problems\, surfacing the perspectives of diverse st
 akeholders\, and finding new pathways forward in situations where expertis
 e is abundant but fragmented. The session is designed for cross-sector lea
 ders grappling with problems too complex for any one discipline to solve a
 lone.\nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/event/what-are-people-for\nFrom Pushpin Bo
 ston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/what-are-people-for
END:VEVENT
