SUMMARY:Starr Forum: AI and Global Power: Democracy\, Competition\, and Con
 trol
LOCATION:MIT\, 70 MEMORIAL DR\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:Jake Sullivan is a former US national security advisor and curr
 ently the Kissinger Professor of the Practice of Statecraft and World Orde
 r at the Belfer Center\, Harvard Kennedy School. He also served as the 28t
 h assistant to the president for national security affairs (national secur
 ity advisor) where he focused on artificial intelligence (AI) as a top nat
 ional security priority. In the Obama administration\, he served as nation
 al security advisor to then-Vice President Biden\, director of the policy 
 planning staff at the U.S. Department of State\, and deputy chief of staff
  to Secretary of State Hillary Clinton.\nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/event/st
 arr-forum-ai-and-global-power-democracy-competition-and-control\nFrom Push
