SUMMARY:Co-Adaptive—Ruth Mandl and Bobby Johnston
LOCATION:MIT\, 134 MASSACHUSETTS Avenue\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:Part of the MIT Fall 2026 Architecture Lecture Series Presented
  with the Architecture and Urbanism Group As our planet gets hotter\, and 
 more extreme weather events become the norm\, CO Adaptive is positioning t
 hemselves as an unbuild\, design and build practice: a new model that reun
 ites designers and builders through collaboration in order to re-think our
  joint role in shaping the built environment\; contending with architectur
 e at the intersection of saving embodied carbon and reducing operational e
 nergy. As stewards of the existing material repository contained in our ci
 ties\, CO Adaptive aims to increase the resilience and reusability of all 
 that already surrounds us.\nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/event/co-adaptiveruth
 -mandl-and-bobby-johnston\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/bosto
 n/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/co-adaptiveruth-mandl-and-bobby-johnston
